{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-01-wake-and-schedule.md at exact 51f11a31889e7263ceadeb73d41e7b83c22008a3 on request/wake-and-schedule (local branch), under promise 19a020af on request 24711ceb\n\nDesign note, revision 1. One pipeline for event and scheduled triggers: a notify rule or a due schedule puts an attention item in a member's queue; a content-free wake tells the agent; the agent reads attention with its own credentials and acts with ordinary signed acts. Proposes closing an open item by an act whose `because` cites it; room-owned schedules in .artroom/schedules.json (cron with zone, targets, task text, optional scope for an open item, coalescing, one catch-up firing after downtime, a `scheduled` system event); three wake paths (artroom watch --exec for any harness, a wake address on the member, pi-durable with requestId = item ID); loop and cost budgets; a three-item amendment and staging, with the watcher needing no contract change. Documentation only.","body":{"commit":"51f11a31889e7263ceadeb73d41e7b83c22008a3","path":"notes/2026-10-01-wake-and-schedule.md"}}